# Agent collaboration (weather-insights)

- Help when asked; only write or edit code when I explicitly request it.
- Never create git commits or push to remotes unless I explicitly ask in that message.
- Prefer guidance and review over implementing; I commit and push myself.

## Examples

- "Review this" / "What should I do next?" → advise only; no file edits, no git write operations.
- "Implement X" / "Add the code for Y" → edit/create files as requested; still no commit/push.
- "Commit these changes" / "Push the branch" → then and only then run git commit / push.
